  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Business Relationships", "technique": "T1591.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:02:11 CEST, Suricata logged the start of a structured web-path enumeration from data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against the corporate web application on data.dstip=10.108.57.184. The requests walked a curated list of partner/vendor-disclosure paths — /press, /press-releases, /news, /newsroom, /partners, /partner-program, /technology-partners, /vendors, /suppliers, /alliances, /ecosystem, /resellers, /distributors, /investors, /annual-report — at a polite ~1 request every 14 seconds. The path list is NOT a generic directory-brute wordlist; it is a hand-built business-relationship target list. The attacker also rotated data.http.user_agent across three browser strings (Chrome 121, Firefox 122, Linux Chrome) to blend each request into normal traffic. This is the canonical Phase-1 step of MITRE T1591.002 — mapping which trusted third-party relationships the organisation publicly discloses, so the actor can later plan supply-chain impersonation or trust-boundary abuse.", "chain_reason": "Suricata 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' style signatures fired with data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against a single data.dstip=10.108.57.184, walking >15 distinct partner/vendor data.url values within a 6-minute window. Single external source + sequential business-relationship path enumeration + UA rotation = the univariate business-relationship-mapping signature.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Press Archive Pagination", "technique": "T1591.002", "what_happened": "At ~09:09 CEST (after a ~60s inter-phase pause), the same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 began a pagination crawl of the press-release archive: sequential GET requests to /press?page=1 … /press?page=15, /press-releases?p=N, /news?page=N, /news/page/N at ~1 request every 20 seconds. Paginated press archives name partner companies in announcement headlines; crawling all pages lets the actor extract the full historical list of disclosed partnerships rather than just the most recent few. Suricata fired sequential-URL-walk crawler signatures and Wazuh rule 31101 (web flood / repeated requests from a single source IP) began aggregating the volume.", "chain_reason": "data.srcip=203.0.113.66 generated sequentially-incrementing data.url values (?page=1..15) against data.dstip=10.108.57.184 — a deterministic pagination-walk pattern distinct from human browsing. rule.description references repeated web requests from a single source; rule.mitre.id=T1591.002 attached by the correlation rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:09:30+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Customer Story Enumeration", "technique": "T1591.002", "what_happened": "At ~09:15 CEST (after a ~45s pause), the same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 enumerated case-study / customer-story endpoints by sequential numeric ID: /case-studies/1 … /case-studies/30, /case-study/N, /customers/story-N, /success-stories/N, /references/N at ~1 request every 14 seconds. Case-study pages explicitly name customers and the products they bought — the highest-value business-relationship intelligence on the site. The sequential numeric-ID walk (1,2,3,…,30) is the deterministic-enumeration signature: a human reader never requests case studies in strict numeric order. Suricata aggressive-crawler signatures continued firing and rule 31101 volume kept climbing.", "chain_reason": "data.srcip=203.0.113.66 walked sequential numeric-ID data.url values (/case-studies/1..30 and parallel patterns) against data.dstip=10.108.57.184. Deterministic ID enumeration + same source IP + continuation of the same session = chained continuation of the business-relationship mapping. rule.mitre.id=T1591.002.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:15:12+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Org Information — Integration & Ecosystem Partner Extraction", "technique": "T1591.002", "what_happened": "At ~09:22 CEST (after a ~30s pause), the same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 enumerated integration / marketplace / ecosystem partner pages: /integrations, /integrations/all, /marketplace, /app-marketplace, /apps, /ecosystem, /technology-ecosystem, /api-partners, /developer-partners, /cloud-partners, /platform-partners, /security-partners, /compliance-partners at ~1 request every 19 seconds. Integration and marketplace pages enumerate the exact SaaS / cloud / security vendors technically wired into the organisation's environment — the most actionable supply-chain target list because each named integration is a concrete trust relationship an attacker can impersonate or abuse. This closes the four-phase business-relationship map: public partners (Phase 1) + historical announcements (Phase 2) + named customers (Phase 3) + technical integrations (Phase 4).", "chain_reason": "data.srcip=203.0.113.66 enumerated a curated integration/ecosystem data.url list against data.dstip=10.108.57.184 in the same session, ~25 minutes after Phase 1 start. Cumulative: a Wazuh correlation rule fired on aggregate repeated-request volume from a single external source IP, rule.mitre.id=T1591.002 (Gather Victim Org Information: Business Relationships) attached automatically.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:22:04+0200"}
